# A missing page gets the site's own 404 page (templates/404.html) instead of
# Apache's plain "Not Found". Added 2026-11-14: the live site was serving the
# Apache default. Checked on the live site after that day's deploy: a missing
# address returns 404 with the site's page, and every other page still
# answers 200, so this host honours the line.
ErrorDocument 404 /404.html
